- [ ] match on ADTs (Option, List, etc.) doesn't work inside defmacro bodies.
      The expansion VM compiles each prelude expression independently via
      compile_program, which starts with an empty known_constructors set.
      So data definitions (e.g. (data (Option a) None (Some a))) don't carry
      constructor knowledge forward to subsequent compilations. In match
      patterns, None/Some are treated as variable patterns instead of
      constructors, causing (Some 5) to match the None branch.
      Workaround: avoid match on Option/List inside macros; use string-contains,
      nil?, car/cdr, etc. instead.
- [ ] equal? broken for Char — values_equal in vm.rs doesn't handle the Char case,
      falls through to false. Chars are NaN-boxed but aren't numbers, bools, nil,
      or objects. Workaround: compare via (= (char-code a) (char-code b)).
- [ ] Inner define doesn't capture enclosing lambda parameters — closures created
      by `define` inside a lambda body fail to capture variables from the enclosing
      lambda's parameters when the closure is later executed in a different handler
      scope (e.g. passed through run-safe/try which runs it in a fresh handle block).
      Workaround: pass captured variables explicitly as function arguments to the
      inner define'd function.
