- [x] What happens to builtin handlers if there's another operation with the same name which belongs to another effect
        Example below has inconsistent results when run multiple times. Sometimes it handles MyIO, sometimes it triggers the exhaustiveness check for io/IO
        ```lisp
        (import "std:io" as io)

        (effect MyIO
          (print (-> Unit String)))

        (handle (perform println "oii")
          ((print m k) -> "Oiii"))
        ```
